## 📌 1. Project Overview

This module demonstrates the practical application of **SQL SET Operators** using the Hospital Patient Management System developed in Microsoft SQL Server.

SET Operators are used to combine or compare the results of two or more SELECT statements and retrieve meaningful information from database tables.

### 🎯 Learning Objectives

- Understand the purpose of SQL SET Operators.
- Combine query results using UNION and UNION ALL.
- Identify common records using INTERSECT.
- Identify differences between query results using EXCEPT.
- Understand duplicate handling in SQL SET Operators.
- Apply SET Operators to real-world hospital business scenarios.

---

## 🏥 2. Types of SQL SET Operators

SQL Server supports four major SET Operators:

| Operator | Purpose |
|---|---|
| UNION | Combines results and removes duplicate rows. |
| UNION ALL | Combines results and retains duplicate rows. |
| INTERSECT | Returns common rows from both results. |
| EXCEPT | Returns rows from the first result that are absent from the second. |

---

## 💻 3. SQL Scripts and Business Scenarios

### 01. UNION Operator

**Business Scenario:** Consolidated Patient Identification.

**Business Requirement:** Retrieve patients registered in Bengaluru and all female patients in one consolidated list.

**Business Objective:** Combine both result sets and eliminate duplicate rows.

**SQL Script:** [01_UNION.sql](./01_UNION.sql)

**Execution Evidence:**

![UNION Result](./Execution_Evidence/Union.PNG)

---

### 02. UNION ALL Operator

**Business Scenario:** Patient List Consolidation.

**Business Requirement:** Combine Bengaluru patients and all female patients while retaining duplicate records.

**Business Objective:** Preserve all records from both SELECT statements.

**SQL Script:** [02_UNION_ALL.sql](./02_UNION_ALL.sql)

**Execution Evidence:**

![UNION ALL Result](./Execution_Evidence/Union_All.PNG)

---

### 03. INTERSECT Operator

**Business Scenario:** Common Patient Identification.

**Business Requirement:** Identify patients who are registered in Bengaluru and are female.

**Business Objective:** Retrieve only the common patient records satisfying both result-set conditions.

**SQL Script:** [03_INTERSECT.sql](./03_INTERSECT.sql)

**Execution Evidence:**

![INTERSECT Result](./Execution_Evidence/Intersect.PNG)

---

### 04. EXCEPT Operator

**Business Scenario:** Patient List Difference.

**Business Requirement:** Identify patients registered in Bengaluru who are not included in the female patient list.

**Business Objective:** Retrieve records from the first SELECT statement that do not exist in the second SELECT statement.

**SQL Script:** [04_EXCEPT.sql](./04_EXCEPT.sql)

**Execution Evidence:**

![EXCEPT Result](./Execution_Evidence/Except.PNG)

